  "description": "Part demolition of existing sports hall and erection of a two storey front and side extension to incorporate new adult education block, including reception, classrooms and creche and extension to sports hall to incorporate new changing facilities, fitness room and gym.",
  "site_name": "Kingsley Academy",
  "last_updated_by": "Northgate M3",
  "decision_target_date": "05/11/2003",
  "borough": "Hounslow",
  "postcode": "TW3 1AX",
  "street_name": "Cecil Road",
  "bo_system": "Northgate M3",
  "development_type": "Major general industry-storage-warehousing",
  "lapsed_date": "24/02/2009",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 0 - .",
    "Condition : 1 - The development hereby permitted shall be begun before the expiration of five years from the date of this permission.",
    "Condition : 2 - No development shall take place until samples of the materials to be used in the construction of the external surfaces of the hereby permitted have been submitted to and approved in writing by the local planning authority.  Development shall be carried out in accordance with the approved details",
    "Condition : 3 - The proposed development shall be carried out in all respects in accordance with the proposals contained in the application and the plans submitted therewith and approved by the Local Planning Authority, or as shall have been otherwise agreed in writing by the Local Planning Authority before the building is occupied.",
    "Condition : 4 - No demolition or construction work shall take place on the site except between the hours of  0800 to 1800 on Mondays to Saturdays and none shall take place on Sundays and public holidays without the prior agreement of the Local Planning Authority.",
    "Condition : 5 - Before commencement of operations, a scheme shall be submitted to and approved by the Local Planning Authority to cover the following matters:\r\n\r\n(i)\tany external illumination of the site\r\n\r\n(ii)\tmeasures to ensure that all mud and other loose materials are not carried on the wheels and chassis of any vehicles leaving the site; and\r\n\r\n(iii)\tmeasures to minimise dust nuisance caused by the operations and to ensure that no dust or other debris is carried on to the adjoining properties.\r\n\r\nThe scheme so approved should be fully implemented.\r\n",
    "Condition : 6 - The use hereby permitted shall not be begun until details of the arrangements for storing of waste and recycled materials have been submitted to and approved by the Local Planning Authority.  The arrangements for storing waste and recycled materials shall not be carried out otherwise than in accordance with any approval given and shall be completed before any part of the accommodation hereby permitted is occupied.",
    "Condition : 7 - The use hereby permitted forsports hall, adult educationcentre and associated educational offices shall not be begun until full particulars and details of a scheme to insulate the premises against the transmission of airborne and impact sound has been submitted to and approved by the Local Planning Authority and the development shall not be carried out otherwise than in accordance with any approval given.",
    "Condition : 8 - There shall be no vehicular or pedestrian access to the school grounds from Cecil Road. The only means of vehicular access to the school shall be from Prince Regent Road, and pedestrian access shall be from Prince Regent Road, with limited and controlled pedestrian access from the car park adjacent to the sports hall.",
    "Condition : 9 - The access doorway to theeducational buildings and sports hall shall have a minimum clear width of 900mm, a level surface or ramp between the pavement and the floor and a door handle of not more than 1m above ground level.",
    "Condition : 10 - No development shall take place within the area indicated on drawing number 726/ED 10 received 11.8.03, until the applicant, or their agents or successors in title, has secured the implementation of a programme of archaeological work in accordance with a written scheme of investigation, including the timetable for the investigation which has been submitted by the applicant and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority."
  ],
